 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "And May is all sweet the flower\nThat makes the dawn so very\nDelightful, and night so dark indeed.\nO summer of old ago!\nI rode thee home. The summer's friend alone\nA world of merry things has he never,\nNor had I heard how long since that hour\nHe set us in these days to do better.\nFair maidens shall we meet again?\nWill love draw nigh? will sorrow?\nShall any born face there be like ours?\nAll we meet will be flowers.",
